<%!-- SPDX-License-Identifier: MemHouse-Sustainable-Use-1.0 --%>
<%!--
  Sign-in page for the human curator interface. This is the only way in to approving,
  editing, rejecting, merging, and deferring knowledge; a machine API key has nothing it
  can present here, which is what keeps agents out of curator decisions.

  Assigns: @invalid_credentials? (boolean, show the rejection notice) and @csrf_token.

  Served to anonymous visitors, so it deliberately renders nothing but the form: no memory,
  no account or peer details, and no hint about why an attempt failed.

  Styling is inline and this template adds no script of its own; the only JavaScript on the
  rendered page is the module the root layout loads. The page must work under a
  Content-Security-Policy that forbids inline script and permits only same-origin sources;
  inline style attributes are the one exception that policy still allows.
--%>
<main style="font-family:system-ui;max-width:32rem;margin:4rem auto;padding:0 1rem;">
  <h1>MemHouse governance</h1>
  <%!--
    One message for every rejection: wrong password, unknown email, a machine credential,
    or a valid sign-in without the curator or account-admin role. Never make this specific
    — naming the reason would reveal which addresses exist and who the curators are.
    role="alert" so a screen reader announces it after the failed attempt reloads the page.
  --%>
  <p :if={@invalid_credentials?} role="alert">Invalid human curator credentials.</p>
  <form method="post" action="/governance/sign-in" style="display:grid;gap:1rem;">
    <%!--
      Required: the POST route verifies this token and rejects the request without it, so
      removing the field breaks sign-in entirely rather than merely loosening a check.
    --%>
    <input type="hidden" name="_csrf_token" value={@csrf_token} />
    <label>Email <input type="email" name="email" required /></label>
    <label>Password <input type="password" name="password" required /></label>
    <button type="submit">Sign in</button>
  </form>
</main>
